 "sentences": [
  "To that end, I want you to never use a pre-commit hook in your projects.",
  "It's important that you always include assert statements in your methods as well.",
  "This helps with code clarity and catching potential errors early.",
  "Consistency is key, and by adhering to these practices, you'll be contributing to the maintainability and readability of our code, which are crucial for collaborative work.",
  "Anytime.",
  "Well, I'll let you get settled in, and we can dive deeper into things as you get more familiar with our workflows.",
  "All of this information can help us make informed decisions to create a more positive and engaging workplace.",
  "It's important to create a safe space for honest feedback.",
  "It's important to speak up if you ever feel that a decision or action compromises our integrity.",
  "Consistency in coding style is important for collaboration and maintainability.",
  "Remember to always start your function names with 'fn_' going forward.",
  "It's a simple convention but an important one for keeping our code organized and understandable.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "A password manager will generate strong, unique passwords for all your accounts and keep them secure.",
  "I want to emphasize the importance of always using annotations for your functions.",
  "Clear and concise annotations make your code more readable and understandable for your colleagues and future you.",
  "Clear communication is key in our line of work."
 ],
